{
	"id": "effect-succeed",
	"text": "Now let's take a look at a few rudimentary Effect constructors. We'll begin with Effect.succeed, which describes a computation that succeeds with the given value. Here we'll give it the string \"pismire\", which was my grandmother's favorite word. This is an Effect<string>. It succeeds with a string, it can never fail, and it has no requirements. Luckily, we can elide trailing nevers, leaving us with a much more readable type ascription.",
